  "description": "Test vectors for the webhook URL guard (design §2.7): admin-api checks a subscription URL on save, meeting-api again on every send (webhooks/ssrf.py). Rules: only http and https; a host is required; a URL that does not parse is refused, and so is a port that is given but is not a number from 1 to 65535, allow-listed host or not; the internal hostnames and the private, loopback, link-local and multicast ranges are refused, an IPv4-mapped IPv6 address (::ffff:a.b.c.d) being judged as the IPv4 address it maps; a DNS name is resolved and refused if it resolves to nothing or if ANY address it resolves to is refused. A host in the allow-list (WEBHOOK_PRIVATE_HOST_ALLOWLIST, compared case-insensitively) is accepted without those checks and without resolving it. 'resolves_to' is what the test resolver returns for the URL's host.",
